# A NEWS File to document package updates

CHANGES IN VERSION 2.21.2
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * ADDIS_exhaustive now checks that lambda >= alpha * tau, as required by
      Fischer et al. (2024); this also ensures no p-value above lambda is
      rejected
    * ADDIS_exhaustive now rejects alpha = 1, lambda = tau and gamma summing
      to more than 1, which previously gave invalid results without an error
    * ADDIS now rejects lambda = tau, as required by Tian and Ramdas (2019)
    * ADDIS with async = TRUE now follows Algorithm 3 of Tian and Ramdas (2019)
      exactly. Rejection times and candidate counts were previously based on the
      order in which tests started rather than on their decision times, which
      gave different (sometimes higher) test levels when tests overlapped
    * LOND now checks that a user-supplied betai is at least as long as the
      number of p-values
    * the default gamma (or beta) sequences based on Javanmard and Montanari
      (2018), equation 31, now use the normalising constant 0.07908197, so that
      they sum to 1; the constant given in the paper (0.07720838) gives a sum of
      about 0.976. This affects the defaults of LOND, LORD, LONDstar, LORDstar,
      Alpha_spending, bonfInfinite, online_fallback and supLORD
    * LORD with version = 'discard' now requires w0 <= tau.discard * alpha, as
      in Tian and Ramdas (2019), and its default w0 is min(alpha/10,
      tau.discard * alpha/2). Previously FDR control could be lost when
      tau.discard < 0.1
    * LORD with version = 'dep' and LORDdep now check the condition of
      Javanmard and Montanari (2018), example 3.7, sum(xi_i * (1 + log(i))) <=
      alpha/b0, instead of sum(xi_i) <= alpha/b0. setBound("LORDdep") now
      returns a sequence satisfying this condition
    * LORD with version = 3 now adds the reward b0 to the wealth at the time of
      each rejection, as in Javanmard and Montanari (2018), equation 9; the
      reward was previously credited two steps late
    * LORD with versions 3 and 'dep' now give an error if w0 >= alpha and b0 is
      not supplied (b0 = alpha - w0 was previously negative)
    * BatchStBH and StoreyBH no longer cap the adjusted p-values at 1, which
      made every hypothesis in a batch rejected when the test level was 1 or
      more
    * SAFFRONstar with version = 'batch' now caps the test levels of the first
      batch at lambda, as for later batches
    * ADDIS_spending with dep = TRUE now sums over j < t - L_t, as in Tian and
      Ramdas (2021), equation 23; the sum previously included one more test,
      and could read past the end of gammai
    * ADDIS, ADDIS_spending, Alpha_investing, LONDstar, LORD, LORDstar,
      online_fallback, SAFFRON and SAFFRONstar now check that a user-supplied
      gammai (or betai) is at least as long as the number of p-values
    * fixed a memory error in LORDstar with version = 'async' for a single
      p-value
    * the checks that gammai (or betai) sums to at most 1 (or alpha) now allow
      for rounding error, so the output of setBound() is always accepted
    * LORD, LORDstar, SAFFRON, SAFFRONstar, ADDIS and Alpha_investing now check
      that a user-supplied gammai is non-increasing, as the source papers
      require
    * the batch versions of LONDstar, LORDstar and SAFFRONstar no longer fail
      when some test levels are exactly zero
    * SAFFRON, SAFFRONstar, BatchStBH, StoreyBH and ADDIS_spending now require
      lambda < 1
    * ADDIS_spending test levels are now capped at lambda, as Tian and Ramdas
      (2021) require
    * StoreyBH now accepts a data frame, as documented, and its help page gives
      the Storey-BH rejection threshold
    * bonfInfinite and LORDdep now use the date-sorted data frame
    * supLORD is much faster: the normalising constant of each rejection's
      spending sequence is computed once rather than at every later step
      (e.g. 6 s to 0.03 s for 1000 p-values with rho = 1000)
    * supLORD now follows Xu and Ramdas (2021) exactly: the boost from the first
      rejection is spent from the next test onwards (previously only after a
      second rejection); the r-th rejection earns b rather than beta0
      (equation 21); the offset a is the root of equation 20 (previously
      searched for only on (0, r/10)); and the spending sequence is computed on
      the log scale, avoiding NaN levels for large eta. These changes increase
      power, in some settings substantially
    * supLORD now accepts rho greater than the number of p-values with the
      default gammai, and checks the length of a user-supplied gammai
    * LORDstar and SAFFRONstar (all versions) are much faster, with identical
      results: the times of known rejections and the counts of candidates are
      updated as tests are made rather than recomputed at every step (e.g.
      LORDstar with version = 'async' takes under 0.01 s rather than 150 s,
      and SAFFRONstar 0.01 s rather than 350 s, for 8000 p-values)
    * all functions now give an error if no p-values remain after missing
      values are removed; several functions previously crashed R for empty or
      all-missing input
    * missing p-values in a data frame now remove only those rows (rows with
      missing values in other columns were also removed), and are an error when
      the data frame has decision times or lags
    * LOND, Alpha_investing and online_fallback now return the id column, as
      LORD, SAFFRON and ADDIS do, so results can be matched to the input after
      the p-values are sorted by date
    * decision times must be finite, and ADDIS with async = TRUE now checks
      them as LONDstar, LORDstar and SAFFRONstar do; decision times larger than
      the integer range were previously treated as already known
    * ADDIS_spending with dep = TRUE gives a clear error if there is no column
      of lags
    * Alpha_spending, BatchBH, BatchPRDS and BatchStBH (and the deprecated
      LORDdep and bonfInfinite) now check that a user-supplied gammai (or xi or
      alphai) is long enough, instead of returning NA levels
    * the default sequence of LORD with version = 'dep' and w0 > b0 no longer
      depends on the number of p-values, and the default for w0 <= b0 uses the
      constant 0.1393066, so that the condition of Javanmard and Montanari
      (2018), example 3.7, holds exactly
    * the progress bars of ADDIS, Alpha_investing, LONDstar, LORD and SAFFRON
      count tests, and no longer overflow for more than 46,340 p-values
    * corrected several error messages
    * added tests of ADDIS_exhaustive testing levels and of the async ADDIS
      candidate threshold
    * corrected errors in the documentation, vignettes and references

CHANGES IN VERSION 2.21.1
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * added the ADDIS_exhaustive procedure and documentation
    * fixed bugs in ADDIS
    * fixed a floating-point precision issue in the LOND check on betai
    * refreshed documentation and pkgdown site for the new release
    * tidied build ignores for development-only files

CHANGES IN VERSION 2.2.0
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * fixed bugs in LONDstar, LORDstar and SAFFRONstar
    * updated code for ADDIS


CHANGES IN VERSION 2.0.0
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * added Rcpp code for online testing algorithms
    * added online batch algorithms of Zrnic et al. [2020]
    * added Storey-BH algorithm
    * added setBound function
    * updated vignette and pkgdown site
    * updated unit tests
    * updated references


CHANGES IN VERSION 1.8.0
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * harmonised inputs to algorithms
    * added unit tests
    * updated authors
    

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.4.0
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * added online FWER algorithms of Tian and Ramdas [2019b]
    * added the ADDIS algorithms of Tian and Ramdas [2019a]
    * added asynchronous online testing algorithms of Zrnic et al. [2018]
    * added the SAFFRON procedure for online FDR control [Ramdas et al., 2018]
    * added the Alpha-investing procedure of Ramdas et al. [2018]
    * updated vignette
    * deprecated LORDdep and added functionality to LORD
    * deprecated bonfInfinite, which is replaced by Alpha_spending
    * removed LORD versions 1 and 2
    * added unit tests
    * updated references
    * updated authors


CHANGES IN VERSION 1.2.0
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * updated unit tests for LOND, LORD, bonfInfinite and LORDdep
    * added the LORD++ procedure for online FDR control [Ramdas et al., 2017]
    * updated references
    * updated vignette
    

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.0.0
-----------------------
MODIFICATIONS:

    * package added to Bioconductor
